# Template for .dev.vars. Copy to .dev.vars and fill in real values.
# This file is committed; .dev.vars is not.
#
# Every secret here must also exist in production (`npx wrangler secret put NAME`)
# and vice versa; the names are kept in step deliberately so local and deployed
# behaviour cannot diverge. Plaintext, non-sensitive config belongs in
# wrangler.jsonc under `vars`, not here.
#
# See .dev.vars.example for what each one is and where it is read.

# Signs and verifies staff and client-portal JWTs.
# Read by: src/middleware/auth.ts, src/routes/auth.ts, src/routes/portal.ts
JWT_SECRET=<random 32+ char string>

# Gates the internal `x-agent-actor` identity header. Never leaves the Worker —
# that is what makes the header unforgeable from outside (SECURITY.md #1).
# Read by: src/middleware/auth.ts, src/agents/slack/index.ts
AGENT_INTERNAL_SECRET=<random 32+ char string>

# Slack app signing secret. Verifies the HMAC over the raw request body before
# any Slack payload is trusted, with a 5-minute replay window (SECURITY.md #2).
# Read by: src/agents/slack/lib/slack.ts
SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=<Slack app > Basic Information > Signing Secret>

# Slack bot OAuth token (xoxb-...), for posting messages back into Slack.
# Read by: src/agents/slack/index.ts, src/utils/slack.ts
SLACK_BOT_OAUTH_TOKEN=xoxb-<Slack app > OAuth & Permissions>

# Cloudflare AI Gateway token. Both agents route their Workers AI calls through
# their own gateway (AI_GATEWAY_ACCOUNTANT / AI_GATEWAY_SLACK in wrangler.jsonc),
# and both gateways have Authenticated Gateway enabled — this is sent as
# `cf-aig-authorization`. Without it the gateway refuses the call before Workers
# AI sees it, so the agents fall back to the direct binding and log that they did.
# Read by: src/utils/model.ts
CF_AIG_TOKEN=<Cloudflare dashboard > AI Gateway > token>

# Resend API key — mail to anyone OUTSIDE the company.
#
# The sixth secret. It exists because this account is on the Workers Free plan,
# where the EMAIL binding reaches verified destination addresses only: free for
# staff, refused for every prospect and client. Resend carries those.
#
# Obtain: resend.com -> API Keys -> Create. Verify a SUBDOMAIN there
# (outreach.godwinausten.org), never the apex — the apex SPF is a hard fail that
# GoDaddy's mailboxes depend on and must not be edited.
#
# Unset, outreach mail is logged rather than sent, and says so in the logs.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Svix signing secret for Resend's delivery webhook.
#
# The seventh secret, and the only one whose absence is a hard refusal rather than a
# degraded mode. POST /api/webhooks/resend is the one unauthenticated route in this
# system that WRITES, so this signature is its entire authorization — accepting
# unsigned events would let anyone mark a bounced message delivered, or a delivered
# one bounced.
#
# Obtain: resend.com -> Webhooks -> add an endpoint pointing at
# https://pleiades.galabs.workers.dev/api/webhooks/resend, then copy its signing
# secret. It starts with `whsec_` and the part after that prefix is base64.
#
# Subscribe the endpoint to: email.sent, email.delivered, email.delivery_delayed,
# email.bounced, email.complained. Do NOT subscribe email.opened or email.clicked —
# those are read receipts, they are excluded from this system deliberately, and the
# handler drops them rather than storing them.
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
